  "payload": "About 1,000 kg fuelled lander (dry mass 340 kg) carrying six payloads, among them the 5 kg TENACIOUS micro-rover; crashed during the landing attempt",
  "delta_v": "Not published; a low-energy transfer with a lunar flyby, out to 1.1 million km from Earth",
  "data_quality": "partial",
  "credit": "© ispace for the mission; ispace's Success-5 and Success-7 releases (2025-02-15, 2025-05-07) for the cruise, its technical cause analysis (2025-06-24) and its External Review Task Force report (2026-03-27) for the cause; Spaceflight Now, Space.com, CBS News and SpacePolicyOnline for the descent; LROC (NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University) for the impact site. Conflicts kept open: the last-contact speed is about 42 m/s (151 km/h) in one report and 187 km/h in another, and is unresolved; LROC's '18:13 UTC' impact time conflicts with the 19:17 UTC scheduled landing and the 18:10 UTC descent start, so it is not used. The impact time is not stated by ispace; the 19:15 UTC used here is derived from the last telemetry (about 105 s before 19:17) and is an estimate. Lander width (2.3 m or 2.5 m), main-engine thrust, Isp and propellant mass were not found.",
